; A c-style enum (an all-fixed-value type choice) as the CONTENT of an encoding-carrying wrapper.
; A c-style enum has no `Deserialize` impl of its own — its try-each-variant sequence is INLINED at
; every use site, because a fieldless Copy enum has nowhere to store an encoding and the sidecar
; therefore lives in the owner's encoding struct. That inline dispatch is the one emission site that
; used `final_exprs` entries as a match PATTERN, and it built the pattern from the wrapper's exprs
; JOINED with the enum's own encoding-field names — while the per-variant probe closure, generated
; with a fresh config, returns only the enum's OWN encodings. Under `--preserve-encodings` that was
; wrong twice over, and both halves are pinned here:
;   bytes_payload  — `bytes .cbor <c-enum>`. The `.cbor` wrapper pushes a CALL expression
;                    (`StringEncoding::from({var}_bytes_encoding)`), which is not legal in pattern
;                    position: E0164 per variant, plus E0308 for the arity.
;   tagged_payload — `#6.42(<c-enum>)`. The tag pushes `Some(tag_enc)`, a perfectly LEGAL pattern —
;                    so this rule isolates the arity defect on its own (E0308 per variant), proving
;                    the break is not specific to `.cbor` payloads.
; Both spellings compiled fine under the default and json profiles (every wrapper-side push is
; preserve-gated, so the pattern was empty there and matched the closure's `Ok(())`); the preserve
; profile is the load-bearing one, which is why this belongs in the all-profile corpus rather than
; beside `tests/core`'s default-profile `enum_payload`.
;
; Homogeneity is structural, not incidental: under `--preserve-encodings` a choice only classifies
; as a c-style enum when `enum_variants_have_same_encoding_var` holds, so sampling the encoding
; fields from the first variant is sound. A mixed-kind choice such as `0 / true` becomes an ordinary
; type-choice enum with its own `Deserialize` impl and never reaches this site.
;
; NOT spelled here: a dedicated no-encoding-fields probe of the pattern split's `Ok(())`/`()`
; edge. The tempting spelling `true / null` never reaches this dispatch at all — a two-arm choice
; with a null arm Option-collapses in `parse_type_choices` rather than becoming an enum, and a
; FIXED inner leaves nothing to put in the collapsed `Option<T>`, so the shape is refused
; gracefully at the collapse site itself (tests/robustness/choice_fixed_null_collapse.cddl; the
; deferred presence-shaped lowering is ledgered in cddl-matrix/roadmap.toml § "Findings — open") —
; so it pins nothing about this site; the empty-list edge is instead covered by these same rules
; under the default/json profiles.
payload_enum = 0 / 1 / 2
cbor_enum_holder = [
  bytes_payload: bytes .cbor payload_enum,
  tagged_payload: #6.42(payload_enum),
]
